  "footnotes": [
    "1h 46m interview on the Essentia Foundation channel, hosted by Hans Busstra, on the release of Glattfelder's book Sapient Cosmos: What a Modern-Day Synthesis of Science and Philosophy Teaches Us About the Emergence of Information, Consciousness, and Meaning.",
    "Glattfelder is a complexity scientist / theoretical physicist visibly embarrassed by his own tribe's uncritical physicalism — the register drifts between physics-seminar and confessional throughout.",
    "The load-bearing move: sober waking consciousness is not the ground truth, but one channelled hallucination among many — structurally continuous with the states shamans, mystics, meditators and psychonauts have reported for 50,000+ years.",
    "The book's provocation (~54:00): if brains channel consciousness rather than produce it, then sufficiently complex AI could too — \"why stop here?\"",
    "Composes with the three earlier videos in this session (Emad on sovereign right to intelligence, the VC on tech decoupling from capital, the solo philosopher on the quiet systems revolution) as the physics-and-mysticism variant of the same anti-reductionist argument. Glattfelder supplies the scientific citations the other three implied.",
    "Closing prescription (Bache-inflected): \"cultivate a little bubble of sanity and happiness and joy\" against a world where \"the pace of destruction just keeps getting faster and faster.\""
  ]
